{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Exclude foreign mileage from 2028 EV Excise Duty calculations",
        "additional_details": "Taxing EVs on total odometer readings forces drivers to pay UK tax for holiday miles driven abroad on foreign roads. Petrol and diesel drivers face no such domestic double-charging, as they pay no UK fuel duty overseas. We believe this penalises EV owners.",
        "background": "Ensure that the upcoming 2028 Electric Vehicle Excise Duty (eVED) framework completely excludes mileage accumulated outside the UK from the pay-per-mile tax calculation.",
